+# Gnome AI and trading (v0.3.91)
+
+## AI
+
+- Delvers retain their previous patrol and village defence AI.
+- Smiths keep within approximately five blocks of their own persisted Anvil claim. They roam inside and around their workshop during the day and continue repairing a missing Anvil through existing repair logic.
+- Growers stay within approximately seven blocks of their own Composter claim and favour reachable spaces beside red or brown mushrooms. Each Grower uses their own claimed mushroom farm, not the nearest unrelated farm.
+- Elders prefer the Y+10 upper circular gallery. They roam within approximately six blocks of a walkable upper-gallery anchor. Defending the village can interrupt their work.
+- The work goal has priority four, between bed sleep priority three and ordinary wandering priority five. At night, Gnome Bed sleep takes precedence. Gnomes may still fight threats.
+- All work goals use standard navigation and do not teleport.
+
+## Trades
+
+Right-click a Smith or Grower during the day to open the vanilla Merchant screen. Any ordinary Gnome assigned a Smith or Grower workstation can trade, not just the dedicated spawn-egg Smith entity. Delvers and Elders do not trade.
+
+The catalogue is currently fixed. Every offer has 16 uses per restock. Offer uses are saved in the Gnome's persistent entity data and restock once per Minecraft day if the workstation claim still exists. There is no reputation, villager leveling or price scaling yet.
+
+Smith trades:
+- Four iron ingots for one emerald.
+- Twelve coal for one emerald.
+- Three emeralds for one iron pickaxe.
+- Three emeralds for one iron axe.
+- Five emeralds for one Smith's Hammer.
+
+Grower trades:
+- Twelve red mushrooms for one emerald.
+- Twelve brown mushrooms for one emerald.
+- One emerald for six red mushrooms.
+- One emerald for six brown mushrooms.
+- Two emeralds for four Glowshrooms.
+- Two emeralds for eight glow berries.
+
+Prices are provisional and can be revised without changing the AI system.
